=== Frequency Tuning Range ===

The resonant frequency is tunable via BST bias voltage (from [[ψ Permittivity]] B2):

:<math>\frac{\Delta\omega_{010}}{\omega_{010}} \approx -\frac{1}{2}\frac{\Delta\varepsilon_\psi}{\varepsilon_\psi} \approx \pm 5\%</math>

At 40 kHz: tuning range ≈ 38–42 kHz. This is the frequency servo window available to the [[Anchor Controller]] (D6) for impedance matching adaptation.

=== Mode Purity ===

A well-designed resonator operates in a single mode. Mode purity is quantified by the ratio of energy in the target mode to total stored energy:

:<math>P_{010} = \frac{U_{010}}{U_{\rm total}} = \frac{|c_{010}|^2}{\sum_{nlm}|c_{nlm}|^2}</math>

where <math>c_{nlm} = \int\psi_{\rm drive}(\mathbf{x})\psi_{nlm}^*(\mathbf{x})\,d^3x</math> are the mode expansion coefficients. Target: <math>P_{010} > 0.90</math> (90% of stored energy in the target mode). Achieved by coupling coil geometry optimisation.

== ψ-Dependent Extensions ==

=== Soliton-Mode Coupling ===

The <math>-\lambda\psi^3</math> nonlinear term couples resonator modes that share spatial overlap. Two modes <math>\psi_{nlm}</math> and <math>\psi_{n'l'm'}</math> exchange energy via:

:<math>\mathcal{M}_{nlm,n'l'm'} = \lambda\int \psi_{nlm}^2(\mathbf{x})\psi_{n'l'm'}^2(\mathbf{x})\,d^3x</math>

For the oblate spheroid, <math>\mathcal{M}_{010,020} \neq 0</math> — the ψ₀₁₀ and ψ₀₂₀ modes share equatorial overlap and exchange energy nonlinearly. At high drive amplitudes (soliton regime), this mode coupling can concentrate energy preferentially in the target mode (parametric amplification of ψ₀₁₀ by driving ψ₀₂₀ at 2ω₀₁₀) or inadvertently excite unwanted modes (spurious mode contamination). The [[Anchor Controller]] (D6) monitors for mode contamination via the bifilar back-EMF spectrum.

=== Biological Resonator Coupling ===

Within Track B, if biological cortical tissue has non-zero <math>\chi_\psi^{\rm (bio)}</math>, the tissue inside the cavity forms part of the resonator's effective medium. The total resonator Q then includes a biological contribution:

:<math>\frac{1}{Q_{\rm total}} = \frac{1}{Q_{\rm shell}} + \frac{1}{Q_{\rm bio}}</math>

If <math>Q_{\rm bio}</math> is high (low-loss coherent tissue), total Q increases above the shell-only value — the operator enhances the resonator. If <math>Q_{\rm bio}</math> is low (high-loss incoherent tissue at baseline), total Q decreases. This would manifest as a measurable Q shift between empty-shell and operator-present measurements — the TML-3 biological Q measurement from [[ψ Quality Factor]] (B5).

== TML Measurement Protocol ==

=== TML-2: Resonator Characterisation ===

# Assemble full [[Psi Stabilizer]] shell with bifilar coil, FBG sensors, ferrofluid system.
# Set BST bias to 0V, ferrofluid H-field to Stabilizer set-point (H = 200 A/m).
# Sweep drive frequency from 30–50 kHz via [[Bifilar Coil Engineering]] (D1) driver. Record back-EMF amplitude and phase (S11 proxy).
# Identify resonant peak: frequency of minimum S11 reflection = <math>\omega_{010}</math>.
# Extract Q from S11 bandwidth: <math>Q_L = \omega_{010}/\Delta\omega_{-3\rm dB}</math>.
# Perform ringdown: drive for 10τ, cut, record amplitude decay. Extract τ and verify <math>Q_\psi = \omega\tau/2 = Q_L</math> (agreement confirms coupling is well-characterised).

'''Pass criteria:''' <math>\omega_{010}/(2\pi) = 38</math>–<math>42</math> kHz; <math>Q_L > 200</math>; ringdown Q agrees with VNA Q within 15%; mode frequency stable to ±50 Hz over 30-minute thermal soak.

=== TML-3: Biological Q Shift ===

Repeat TML-2 characterisation with trained operator seated inside [[Psi Stabilizer]] in Standby mode. Compare Q_total and ω_010 against empty-shell baseline. Sham control: identical protocol with shell present but operator absent (seated outside the shell at same distance).

